CLUB: SEMARA SOUTHEASTERN MASS AMATEUR RADIO ASSOCIATION
SOAPBOX: That was great fun. It was my first CQ WW RTTY and my first contest with my new IC-7300Mk2. Unfortunately, a 3-day storm hit on Friday that broke my 80m skyloop. I lifted the ends off the ground and used the tuner. Launching 100W into that bent long wire and my hexbeam seemed to do just fine.
SOAPBOX: Considering how lousy propagation has been recently, Saturday was very good and Sunday varied from good to fair. 10m was terrible. Europe on 40/20 was blasting in for hours with wall-to-wall strong signals. A relatively few Central/South American stations popped up Sat/Sun afternoons and I had no luck working the few VK/JAs that I heard. Solar cycle blues.
SOAPBOX: Until next time… 73s.
